  - [1mExact cut[0m — ~3 lines, fully deterministic output length, no edge cases. Costs you mid-word slices, which look sloppy
    in prose. Cheap to change later.
  - [1mWord boundary + hard-cut fallback[0m — ~6 lines. Clean breaks on prose; falls back to the exact cut when the window
    holds no whitespace, so it's strictly a superset of the first behavior. The only added cost is the fallback branch
    and a test for it.
  - [1mWord boundary, pure[0m — rejected. Without the fallback, [38;5;153mformat("Antidisestablishmentarianism", {maxLength: 10})[39m
    returns [38;5;153m"..."[39m, which is a bug, not a UX choice.

  Two smaller decisions that are harder to change later because they're observable in output:

  - [1mThe [38;5;153m'...'[39m counts toward [38;5;153mmaxLength[0m, so the result never exceeds it. That matches [38;5;153m_.truncate[39m and CSS [38;5;153mtext-overflow[39m,
    and it means "max length" is an actual guarantee rather than "max length plus three". Strings at or under the limit
    pass through untouched.
  - [1mTruncation runs after the case transforms but before [38;5;153mprefix[39m/[38;5;153msuffix[0m, matching the existing chain order — so
    decorators you explicitly asked for are never eaten. Side effect: prefix + suffix can push the final string past
    [38;5;153mmaxLength[39m. The alternative (truncate last) protects the total but can chop your own suffix off, which is worse.

  [1mMy recommendation: word boundary with hard-cut fallback.[0m You said better UX is the goal, the fallback removes the only
  real failure mode, and the extra cost is three lines and one test.

  [1mShort design:[0m add one block to [38;5;153mformat()[39m in [38;5;153mformat.js[39m, guarded on [38;5;153mtypeof options.maxLength === 'number'[39m. If
  [38;5;153mresult.length <= maxLength[39m, leave it. Otherwise slice to [38;5;153mmaxLength - 3[39m, look for the last space in that slice; if
  found, trim back to it; if not, keep the hard slice. Append [38;5;153m'...'[39m. Then add [38;5;153mconsole.assert[39m lines to [38;5;153mformat.test.js[39m in
  the existing style covering: under-limit passthrough, exact-limit passthrough, word-boundary cut, single-long-word
  fallback, and interaction with [38;5;153mprefix[39m. No new files, no dependencies.
